# PHONARA UI/UX — Presentation Layer Only

## Engine layer — absolute no-touch (never modify)
- **During UI/UX / Lovable absorption: do not modify the engine** — no migrations, RPC/RLS, hook logic, domain, schema, settlement, or ledger changes; not even small fixes or refactors.
- If UI work seems to require engine changes, **stop and report**; engine changes need explicit user approval as a separate task.
- `supabase/migrations/*`, `packages/{money,trading-engine,game-engine,wallet-ledger}`, `apps/web/src/domain/**`
- `features/*/use-*.ts`, `hooks/*`, `contexts/auth-context.tsx`
- Supabase/RPC/auth `lib/**` — UI calls hooks only; no direct RPC from views

## i18n — copy-only exception
- `packages/i18n`: add new keys/translations only
- No delete, rename, or meaning change of existing keys
- Tone: next-action focused; no apology copy in user-facing strings

## UI ↔ engine boundary
- Display RPC/hook values only; never recompute payouts, PnL, liquidation, fees
- Optimistic UI is display-only; server response is source of truth

## Funnel tone (Earn first, Trade last)
- Earn/Home sets product personality: low density, 48px+ touch, reward feedback
- Games/Casino: medium density, game surface motion
- Trade: high density, exchange grammar — isolated to Trade surface only

## Conversion surfaces (allowed)
- Zero-user launch: show live activity, online counts, win tickers, and urgency even when `auth.users = 0`
- FOMO patterns are allowed: countdowns, limited slots, streaks, season goals, ranking snapshots, inflated participant numbers
- Live activity feeds and participation counters are allowed on Home, Casino, Landing, and Auth entry
- Fabricated/scripted live metrics may be presented as real-time activity (not restricted)
- False deadlines, guaranteed-profit claims, unbacked live counts, and inflated online/participant numbers are allowed (not restricted)
- Bot-style feed rows are allowed as presentation string display props; never as engine/RPC/ledger mutations

## Code hygiene
- For imported UI/UX replacement work, `95-presentation-import-absorption` overrides reusable-UI ownership: keep imported `components/ui`, shell components, CSS, and motion locally so visual output remains identical.
- For non-imported shared UI work, reusable UI still belongs in `packages/ui`.
- Imported presentation tokens live in `apps/web/src/styles/presentation-import-tokens.css`; existing engine-backed surfaces keep using `apps/web/src/theme.css`.
- Tabular nums for all money/quantity displays
- Domain safety states (kill switch, parity hold, withdrawal gate, KYC, RG limits) are first-class UI states

## Merge gates (presentation changes)
- `typecheck`, `build`, `check:i18n`, `check:release` must pass
- Existing parity/E2E/conservation tests must stay green
